[["text","LESSON 22 / 31 • ADDITIONAL INTERVIEW TOPIC"],["heading","22. Tree traversals"],["text","English: Preorder, inorder, postorder and level-order visit nodes in different sequences."],["sinhala","","සිංහල: Tree nodes බ9න පිළිJවෙළ Jවෙනස් traversal methods තිJයනවො.",359],["text","Real-world example: Sorted BST output"],["code","Tree: 2 with children 1,3"],["code","Pre: 2,1,3 | In: 1,2,3 | Post: 1,3,2"],["heading","Java example / illustration"],["code","// Method inside a class\nvoid inorder(TreeNode n) {\n  if (n == null) return;\n  inorder(n.left);\n  System.out.println(n.key);\n  inorder(n.right);\n}"],["heading","Complexity and trade-offs"],["text","Time O(n); recursive stack O(h)."],["heading","Interview question"],["heading","Which traversal sorts a BST?"],["text","Inorder traversal."],["heading","Quick practice"],["text","Explain this concept aloud, trace the example, and describe when you would choose this"],["text","structure over an alternative."]]